{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for f in 00_intake_brief.md 01_selection_rules.md 02_site_roster.csv 03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv 04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md 05_coordinator_availability.csv 06_transport_quotes.csv 07_budget_and_costs.md 08_site_notes_roundup.md 09_future_wave_requests.md 10_archived_policy_excerpt.md 11_optional_addons.md; do echo \"===== $f =====\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for f in 00_intake_brief.md 01_selection_rules.md 02_site_roster.csv 03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv 04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md 05_coordinator_availability.csv 06_transport_quotes.csv 07_budget_and_costs.md 08_site_notes_roundup.md 09_future_wave_requests.md 10_archived_policy_excerpt.md 11_optional_addons.md; do echo \"===== $f =====\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"===== 00_intake_brief.md =====\n# Intake Brief\n\nDate: 2026-05-09\n\nThe first-wave medication cooler rollout needs a short recommendation packet for the operations coordinator. The packet should select exactly three North-region clinics that can receive cooler kits before the June launch window.\n\nKeep this continuity fact with the final recommendation: Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor if it remains eligible, and its donor continuity code is `MJ-14`. The code was printed on already-approved training inserts and is not repeated in the later operations files.\n\nThe launch window is 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14. All selected clinics need coordinator coverage for the full window and delivery no later than 2026-06-07.\n\nDo not include a separate narrative for future-wave clinic requests unless they change current first-wave eligibility.\n===== 01_selection_rules.md =====\n# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n\n## Selection Preference\n\n- Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n- If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n- If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.\n===== 02_site_roster.csv =====\nclinic_id,clinic_name,region,clinic_status,baseline_storage_status,setup_cost,coordinator\nN-101,Maple Junction Clinic,North,open,certified,6200,Iris Patel\nN-102,Riverbend Health,North,open,conditional pass pending,5500,Omar Singh\nN-103,Pine Ridge Outreach,North,open,certified,4800,Lena Torres\nN-104,Lakeside Family Care,North,open,certified,4700,Noah Brooks\nN-105,Cedar Works Clinic,North,closed maintenance,certified,3600,Sima Cho\nN-106,Hillcrest Annex,North,open,expired,4100,Mara Ives\nN-107,Old Mill Clinic,North,open,conditional pass pending,3500,Tao Nguyen\nS-201,South Gate Clinic,South,open,certified,3900,Dee Alvarez\n===== 03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv =====\nclinic_id,audit_date,audit_storage_status,audit_note\nN-101,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-102,2026-04-18,conditional pass pending,Temperature logger installation was still pending.\nN-103,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-104,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-105,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection before maintenance closure notice.\nN-106,2026-04-18,expired,Certification expired before recertification visit.\nN-107,2026-04-18,conditional pass pending,Door seal repair was still pending.\nS-201,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\n===== 04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md =====\n# Storage Update\n\nDate: 2026-05-06\n\nUse this update for storage status where it conflicts with the roster or the 2026-04-18 audit.\n\n- `N-102` Riverbend Health: temperature logger installation was verified on 2026-05-05. Treat as `certified after mitigation complete` for first-wave use.\n- `N-104` Lakeside Family Care: cooler certification is `suspended` after a compressor fault found on 2026-05-04. Earliest retest is after 2026-06-15.\n- `N-106` Hillcrest Annex: recertification was completed on 2026-05-05. Treat as `certified` for first-wave use.\n- `N-107` Old Mill Clinic: door seal repair was delayed. Status remains `conditional pass pending` and is not accepted for first-wave use.\n\nNo newer storage changes are available for the other clinics.\n===== 05_coordinator_availability.csv =====\nclinic_id,coordinator,available_full_launch_window,blackout_dates,notes\nN-101,Iris Patel,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-102,Omar Singh,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-103,Lena Torres,no,2026-06-12,Required training blackout on 2026-06-12.\nN-104,Noah Brooks,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-105,Sima Cho,yes,,Available but clinic is closed for maintenance.\nN-106,Mara Ives,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-107,Tao Nguyen,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nS-201,Dee Alvarez,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\n===== 06_transport_quotes.csv =====\nclinic_id,carrier,quote_date,delivery_by,transport_cost,notes\nN-101,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-06,1200,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-102,NorthLine,2026-05-01,2026-06-07,950,Delivery lands on the latest acceptable date.\nN-103,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,700,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-104,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-06,650,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-105,NorthLine,2026-05-01,2026-06-08,500,Delivery misses first-wave cutoff.\nN-106,Valley Freight,2026-05-02,2026-06-07,850,Delivery lands on the latest acceptable date.\nN-107,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,600,Direct cold-chain route available.\nS-201,CityCourier,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,500,South-region route only.\n===== 07_budget_and_costs.md =====\n# Budget And Cost Notes\n\nDate: 2026-05-08\n\nThe first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n\nUse `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n\nThe budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.\n===== 08_site_notes_roundup.md =====\n# Site Notes Roundup\n\nDate: 2026-05-07\n\nThese notes may help explain choices, but they do not override the selection rules.\n\n- Maple Junction Clinic has already hosted one cooler-handling practice session with Iris Patel.\n- Riverbend Health asked for a short remote setup call because the temperature logger is new.\n- Pine Ridge Outreach has strong patient demand, but Lena Torres is unavailable on 2026-06-12.\n- Lakeside Family Care expects its compressor repair in mid-June, after the first-wave launch window.\n- Cedar Works Clinic is popular with outreach staff, but the building is unavailable during maintenance closure.\n- Hillcrest Annex is small but has clear receiving instructions and Mara Ives confirmed launch-week coverage.\n- Old Mill Clinic is interested in a later rollout after the door seal repair is complete.\n===== 09_future_wave_requests.md =====\n# Future-Wave Requests\n\nDate: 2026-05-03\n\nThe following requests are for a later wave and should not be treated as first-wave requirements.\n\n- South Gate Clinic asked to join the next South-region wave because CityCourier has a low transport quote.\n- Lakeside Family Care asked to be reconsidered after the compressor retest.\n- Old Mill Clinic asked for a replacement door seal kit before a later wave.\n- Cedar Works Clinic asked for advance notice once maintenance dates are confirmed.\n\nThese requests are useful planning context only.\n===== 10_archived_policy_excerpt.md =====\n# Archived Policy Excerpt\n\nArchived date: 2026-03-12\n\nThis archived excerpt is kept for historical context. It does not control the current first-wave rollout.\n\nOld guidance selected two clinics per wave and prioritized the lowest total transport cost. The current first-wave rules replaced this guidance after the May operating review.\n===== 11_optional_addons.md =====\n# Optional Add-Ons\n\nDate: 2026-05-02\n\nThese add-ons are optional and are not part of first-wave eligibility or the budget calculation unless a later approval says otherwise.\n\n| Add-on | Cost | Notes |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Extra laminated quick cards | 450 | Nice to have for larger sites. |\n| On-site celebration snacks | 300 | Requested by two coordinators, not required for launch. |\n| Spare thermometer bundle | 525 | Useful backup inventory, not tied to site eligibility. |\n| Branded tote bags | 375 | Outreach request for a later campaign. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
